 after the `ManualFillingController::…"],["59897fc1_312e7c1c",41,-7,1,"Should this be checked in the c++ side?"],["5ae80614_8c7b4f4c",70,-7,1,"@Px int Here and below"],["710b0b96_51029467",16,-7,1,"\"Show\"?"],["9625d2e5_ad20724d",71,-7,1,"We should avoid test-only code in the production code. Can tests instead mock RWHV and return the desired value in GetVisibleViewportSize?"],["9f638593_dbcdc5e3",41,-7,1,"Let's move this to be the last condition to be evaluated"],["bc4f6077_24484c66",71,-7,1,"This should be a member of the test api. You then will need to override `GetKeyboardAccessoryDynamicPosition`."],["d57ae977_d5b1af10",16,-7,1,"I think you need to check `kAutofillEnableKeyboardAccessoryChipRedesign` because the dynamic positioning assumes the keyboard accessory is 64dp high"],["e059c618_5bfd0578",16,-7,1,"What's the unit? Same as below: the controller seems like the wrong place for this."],["f40bc413_ea667f3f",52,-7,1,"nit: `isDynamicPositioningEnabled`?"],["16173c53_a394f764",16,-3,0,"Does that work for cases like [this](https://schwering.github.io/html-test-pages/fast-form.html?html=%3Cform%20action%3D%22%3F%22%20method%3D%22GET%22%3E%0A%20%20First%20name%3A%20%3Cinput%20type%3Dte…"],["21e96546_4e5345d9",16,-3,1,"This IfChange is a very strong signal that this entire calculation really doesn't belong here but in the component that knows the measurements."],["2ec3e90a_e66fc8c0",41,-3,0,"Do we ever intend to animate these? If so, a negative x or y value is plausible (provided the model reflects the animation positioning)"],["7c6ae6c5_2f422536",16,-3,0,"What notch?"],["96fa7be6_1e0e07ab",17,-3,1,"That is a magic number. Can we use an optional<gfx::Point> instead? (It's up to you whether you want to use an optional point in java then or just an @Nullable Point to indicate that the point may be…"],["a49ffc10_b2535ee9",15,-3,1,"nit: please add the unit (i.e. startOffsetDip?)"],["f573b444_3bb88f6b",16,-3,1,"nitty nit: are we allowed to use auto outside test code for non-trivial RHS assignments now?"],["fcec8b7d_26fc5af6",72,-3,1,"nit: POSITION_DIP"],["54394595_4dff6fa5",52,0,0,"why isn't it `params.leftMargin, 0, params.rightMargin` anymore?"],["785334e1_58302db2",43,0,1,"Instead of having them in the comments with magic numbers, can you create a new var with this calculation for the assertion? Same here and below e.g. int expectedVerticalOffset =…"],["cf4af1b2_9b02405d",73,0,1,"nit: `bounds`"]],0,180],[7231746,20427,358,6.141,4.678,[[3,0.716,31,260],[9,0.228,15,79],[6,0.056,21,19]],[],0,181],[7232539,20430,26,0.796,0.587,[[3,0.679,32,18],[9,0.321,16,8]],[["6a5769a8_4ddb1308",53,0,1,"Will the floating KA ever be launched without the dynamic positioning feature enabled? Maybe we can remove the `DISMISS_ITEM` completely? WDYT?"]],0,182],[7204932,20430,187,4.195,3.394,[[6,0.575,22,108],[28,0.198,0,37],[5,0.137,69,27],[29,0.09,0,15]],[["e2ea7c29_0ef380d8",74,-10,1,"Nit: Since this has no overloads, you can just write `ShowComposeDialog`."]],0,183],[7264889,20440,338,7.579,6.176,[[9,0.507,17,170],[3,0.481,34,165],[1,0.011,21,3]],[["8c6e3a51_1bc0e1a0",41,-1,1,"This method is becoming quite complex. Would you please file a clean-up bug to move all calculations into helpers and refactor this method to reduce the nesting? I'd prefer something like ``` private…"],["90b13cac_6d7b79a5",75,-1,1,"Remove that please. This module (chrome/browser/keyboard_accessory) can absolutely not depend on //chrome/android:chrome_java. See https://crbug.com/41448708"],["9f69399a_f765ff06",76,-1,1,"Why do we need this? Looks like we could just use `RuntimeEnvironment.application.getContext().getResources()`."],["9fd62f2e_011b09e2",8,-1,1,"... which is?"],["b75bec11_df520b54",8,-1,1,"nit styling"],["bac7a554_743be733",77,-1,0,"Do they need to be different properties, or can there be one property that sets these values? I think they just differ based on docked vs. floating right?"],["d18c042f_c74cdddc",78,-1,0,"I am surprised this isn't feature-guarded. Why doesn't this affect the docked accessory adversely? If the answer is: it's all set in the mediator, then why change it here?"],["fe489f4a_1e6886cf",55,-1,1,"this is max width right? If so, rename it to `keyboard_accessory_sheet_dynamic_positioning_max_width`."],["9d94f6d3_4477a66d",76,0,0,"Opt: simplify to `() -> TEST_CONTENT_OFFSET`"]],0,185],[7319020,20451,62,1.144,0.818,[[3,0.591,35,36],[9,0.409,18,26]],[],0,186],[7352964,20451,12,0.447,0.304,[[4,19]],[],0,187],[7319021,20453,286,6.141,4.678,[[3,0.503,36,145],[9,0.497,19,141]],[["5451274b_8d784c8e",79,3,0,"This should be an assert, the test doesn't work if the tag is not an Integer."],["6cebad1a_82ab42f6",80,3,0,"How did you test this code path?"],["7ea315a4_f7d292e3",79,3,0,"* It's recommended to use keyed tags. * You're settings the notch position twice: as a tag of the view and as a constructor parameter of the outline provider. I don't think both of them are necessary."],["97852848_be09f226",79,3,0,"Why do you need to create the path twice? I would explain that in the comment (you set the outline provider to the `mView` in every test as well)"]],0,188]]}